C o m p i l a t i o n


      Special-Event Park-and-Ride Planning Problem
      CEE 6410/5410
      David Rosenberg
      October 10, 2026
       
      This problem was contributed by Dr. Ran Sun and expanded by Dr. David Rosenberg
       
      Learning objectives.
      Students will be able to:
      •   Define dimensions, decision variables and an objective function;
      •   Formulate demand, capacity, and service-quality constraints;
      •   Solve a small linear program;
      •   Identify constraints;
       
      Problem Statement
      State Department of Transportation guidance for special events emphasizes advance parklotanning for transportation demand, traffic, parking, transit operations, and seating.
       
      Passengers must also be assigned in full bus-loads of 50 passengers per bus.
       
      Additionally, the event parklotanners must rent and bring in grandstands for the attendees. They have 2 potential venders. Each vender has an up-front reservation cost, number of seats per grandstand, and cost to load, ship, and setup a grandstand.
       
      Vendor  Reservation cost ($)    Seats per grandstand    Cost to load, ship, and setup ($ per grandstand)
      PurpleRain $1,000                   100                 200
      Blue Sky    $1,500                  200                 300
       
      Full details at https://usu.instructure.com/courses/818402/files/100525844?wrap=1
       
      David E Rosenberg
      david.rosenberg@usu.edu
  32   
  33  * 1. DEFINE the SETS
  34  SETS parklot Parking Lots /north, south, west/
  35       vendor Vendors of grandstands /PurpleRain, BlueSky/;
  36   
  37  * 2. DEFINE input data
  38  PARAMETERS
  39     MaxPassengers(parklot) maximimum number of peoparklote parking lot can handle (Number)
  40           /north 600,
  41            south 500,
  42            west  600/
  43     Cost(parklot) cost per passenger from parking lot ($ per person)
  44            /north 4,
  45            south 5,
  46            west  7/
  47     TravelTime(parklot) Travel time from parking lot (minutes)
  48           /north 20,
  49            south 12,
  50            west  8/
  51     MaxAverageTime Maximum average travel time for all pasengers (minutes) /13/
  52     Attendees number of attendees /1200/
  53     ReservationCost(vendor) Cost to reserve grandstands from vendor ($)
  54          /PurpleRain 1000,
  55           BlueSky    1500/
  56     Seats(vendor) Seats per grandstand (number)
  57          /PurpleRain 100,
  58           BlueSky    200/
  59     UnitCost(vendor) Cost per grandstand to load ship and setup ($ per grandstand)
  60          /PurpleRain 200,
  61           BlueSky    300/
  62     MaxGrandstands(vendor) max grandstands needed
  63           /PurpleRain 12, BlueSky 6/;
  64   
  65  * 3. DEFINE the variables
  66  VARIABLES   I(vendor) binary decision to use or not use each vendor (1=yes 0=no)
  67              G(vendor) number of granstands ordered
  68              X(parklot) number of buses from parking lots
  69              TCOST  total capital and operating costs ($);
  70   
  71  BINARY VARIABLES I;
  72  INTEGER VARIABLES X,G;
  73   
  74  * 4. COMBINE variables and data in equations
  75  *EQUATIONS
  76  EQUATIONS
  77      ObjectiveFunct  total cost of everything
  78      MaxCap(parklot) max capacity in each lot
  79      TotalDemandCap meet total attendee capacity
  80      GrandSeatsCap meet capacity for grandstand seats
  81      AvgTravel average travel time from lots
  82      VendorMax(vendor) relationship between grandstands and vendor
  83      VendorMin(vendor) min requirment for grandstands if vendor is selected;
  84   
  85  ObjectiveFunct..   TCOST =E= SUM(parklot, Cost(parklot) * 50 * X(parklot)) + SUM(vendor, ReservationCost(vendor) * I(vendor)) + SUM(vendor, UnitCost(vendor) * G(vendor));
  86  MaxCap(parklot)..  50 * X(parklot) =L= MaxPassengers(parklot);
  87  TotalDemandCap..   SUM(parklot, 50 * X(parklot)) =G= Attendees;
  88  GrandSeatsCap..    SUM(vendor, Seats(vendor) * G(vendor)) =G= Attendees;
  89  AvgTravel..        SUM(parklot, (TravelTime(parklot) - MaxAverageTime) * X(parklot)) =L= 0;
  90  VendorMax(vendor).. G(vendor) =L= MaxGrandstands(vendor) * I(vendor);
  91  VendorMin(vendor).. G(vendor) =G= I(vendor);
  92   
  93  * 5. DEFINE the MODEL from the EQUATIONS
  94  MODEL SpecialEvent /ALL/;
  95   
  96  * 6. Solve the Model as a Mixed Integer Program
  97  SOLVE SpecialEvent USING MIP MINIMIZING TCOST;
  98   
  99  * 7. Display the decision variable values in the list file
 100  DISPLAY X.L, I.L, G.L, TCOST.L;
 101   
 102  * Dump all input data and results to a GAMS gdx file
 103  Execute_Unload "MIP-SpecialEvent.gdx";
 104  * Dump the gdx file to an Excel workbook
 105  Execute "gdx2xls MIP-SpecialEvent.gdx"


